  "lineage": "Music of the Bakhtiari, a Luri-speaking tribal confederation of the central Zagros whose seasonal pastures span Chaharmahal and Bakhtiari and Khuzestan. Its repertoire includes lyrical and heroic songs, women's mourning laments (gagriveh), and outdoor dance music for weddings and celebrations played on sorna and dohol, with the kamancheh accompanying songs; the Mahoor Institute has issued regional anthologies.",
